    "Workings"
    "Week 1's cohort, back the same week · actors query"
    button [workings-close] label="Close workings (W)"
      "Close"
    div [station:emit]
      "Emit"
      "no Rust type yet"
      "signed_up"
      "arrives with named properties and no Rust type, so a typo in a property name becomes a new property instead of an error. Declaring it as a struct fixes that, and makes each one smaller to send."
      div [code]
        div [code-line]
          "1"
          span [code-text]
            "//"
            "No"
            "Rust"
            "type"
            "yet."
            "One"
            "written"
            "from"
            "the"
            "properties"
            "it"
            "arrives"
            "with"
            ":"
        div [code-line]
          "2"
          span [code-text]
            "#[derive(Event)]"
        div [code-line]
          "3"
          span [code-text]
            "struct"
            "SignedUp"
            "{"
        div [code-line]
          "4"
          span [code-text]
            "}"
        button [copy] label="Copy as Rust"
          "Copy"
    div [station:send]
      "Send"
      "the wire"
      "What one event weighs is measured from a real one, and none has arrived yet."
      "Waiting for a"
      "signed_up"
      "to weigh."
    div [station:store]
      "Store"
      "events, person_distinct_ids, person_overrides on sqlite"
      "Events land in"
      "events"
      "as they arrive; sessions and persons are kept up to date beside them as each batch is stored, so a query reads tables, never a queue. These are the ones this query read."
